Changes
-------

The copy differs from the original packages in the ways below. The history
of the repository holds each change with its diff.

- The import paths `marker.`, `surya.`, and `pdftext.` are rewritten to
  `raw2md_engine.marker.`, `raw2md_engine.surya.`, and
  `raw2md_engine.pdftext.`.
- The parts that raw2md does not call are removed: the LLM pass, the
  extraction converter, the config parser, the input formats other than
  PDF, the output formats other than Markdown, and the command-line and
  browser applications.
- The PDF converter builds its provider and its Markdown renderer
  directly.
- The settings are fixed values. They do not load from environment
  variables or from a `local.env` file.
- The copy downloads nothing: no font when the converter starts and no
  model weights. `marker/models.py` takes the folder of the weights from
  its caller.
- The models build their non-persistent buffers on the CPU, and the
  loaders build them again after the load of the weights, before the move
  to the device (2026-10-19). Changed files, under
  src/raw2md_engine/surya/: `common/load.py`, `common/adetr/decoder.py`,
  `common/surya/decoder/__init__.py`, `common/surya/encoder/__init__.py`,
  `ocr_error/model/encoder.py`, `foundation/loader.py`,
  `table_rec/loader.py`, and `ocr_error/loader.py`.

Each changed file of `pdftext/` carries a notice at its top.

